 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to waiving the residency\nrequirement for the commissioner of planning, development, and public\ntransportation for Putnam county",
    "basePrintNo": "S6062",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6062-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6062\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nWaives the residency requirement for the commissioner of planning,\ndevelopment, and public transportation for Putnam county\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 3 of public officers law to exempt the county\nof Putnam from the requirement mandating the commissioner of planning,\ndevelopment, and public transportation to reside in Putnam County.\n\nSection 2 states the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Putnam Commissioner of Planning, Development, and Public Transporta-\ntion plays an essential role in driving economic growth by directing\nmillions of dollars into the local economy-indirectly touching the lives\nof all residents of the county. Putnam has been searching for a candi-\ndate to fill this role since June of 2022, a process made difficult due\nto the residency requirement that the commissioner must meet.\n\nPutnam County does not have a large population, therefore it has been\nincredibly difficult to find a person who can fill this unique and\nspecialized position. Candidates in adjoining counties who are otherwise\nqualified should not be excluded from consideration simply because they\nlive, or have relocated outside of Putnam. This legislation comes at the\nrequest of the County Executive.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
